WEBVTT

00:00:05.610 --> 00:00:07.850
We're in front of the Nakasugi police station.

00:00:07.850 --> 00:00:12.780
Just now, the serial kidnapper has been arrested.

00:00:13.510 --> 00:00:17.600
The kidnapper is Shimada Nobuyuki, a 24 year old unemployed man.

00:00:17.600 --> 00:00:21.160
According to the police, he seems willing to testify and has confessed to most of the charges.

00:00:21.570 --> 00:00:22.810
Twenty four...

00:00:24.660 --> 00:00:26.790
Well, sorry, owner.

00:00:27.440 --> 00:00:29.810
We made you stay quite a while.

00:00:32.000 --> 00:00:35.210
Thank you for your cooperation,

00:00:35.210 --> 00:00:41.150
not only with the surveillance but also in the investigation.

00:00:41.150 --> 00:00:41.640
Not at all.

00:00:42.030 --> 00:00:43.260
And...

00:00:43.260 --> 00:00:50.300
we're not going to reveal that the kidnapper was buying your cakes,

00:00:50.300 --> 00:00:51.150
so please don't worry about that.

00:00:52.140 --> 00:00:57.560
We'll also conceal the fact that you reported the crime.

00:00:58.760 --> 00:00:59.370
Owner?

00:00:59.970 --> 00:01:01.450
Is anything wrong?

00:01:01.450 --> 00:01:03.120
Oh, nothing.

00:01:03.560 --> 00:01:04.660
Well then...

00:01:05.480 --> 00:01:08.160
Excuse me.

00:01:08.160 --> 00:01:09.630
Tachibana-san.

00:01:10.030 --> 00:01:12.050
You did great!

00:01:14.040 --> 00:01:17.550
Shimada said you were scary.

00:01:17.550 --> 00:01:22.180
He felt he could never disobey your orders.

00:01:22.180 --> 00:01:26.980
But after all, what I did was trespassing, wasn't it?

00:01:26.980 --> 00:01:30.090
No, not at all! You should receive a commendation.

00:01:30.090 --> 00:01:35.450
Shimada was going to kill the boy
right after making him eat that cake.

00:01:39.570 --> 00:01:43.490
I probably shouldn't say this to you,

00:01:44.270 --> 00:01:48.610
but he said that feeding the children cake was a ceremony,

00:01:48.610 --> 00:01:52.290
so that the kids would go to heaven peacefully.

00:02:09.980 --> 00:02:11.220
Officer.

00:02:11.220 --> 00:02:13.580
No... Akutagawa-san.

00:04:15.210 --> 00:04:17.100
Oh, how about some tea?

00:04:17.100 --> 00:04:18.820
Well, then I'll do it.

00:04:19.190 --> 00:04:20.900
Are you hungry?

00:04:20.900 --> 00:04:23.160
If so, I'll make something.

00:04:23.160 --> 00:04:26.320
I think Tachibana will be hungry too.

00:04:28.400 --> 00:04:28.960
Young master!

00:04:28.960 --> 00:04:29.810
Tachibana.

00:04:29.810 --> 00:04:30.700
Gramps.

00:04:33.490 --> 00:04:35.320
Sorry for being late.

00:04:35.320 --> 00:04:37.280
Are the preparations for tomorrow done?

00:04:37.280 --> 00:04:38.970
Yeah. We're done.

00:04:38.970 --> 00:04:40.130
As usual.

00:04:40.740 --> 00:04:43.220
Did you come back here after going home?

00:04:43.570 --> 00:04:45.050
Because...

00:04:45.050 --> 00:04:48.020
Young master, you weren't hurt, were you?

00:04:48.020 --> 00:04:49.640
Come on!

00:04:49.640 --> 00:04:50.880
Anyway, you guys are dismissed.

00:04:50.880 --> 00:04:52.330
Dismissed.

00:04:52.330 --> 00:04:55.070
Ono and Eiji, don't you have to come in early tomorrow?

00:04:56.470 --> 00:04:57.500
What?

00:04:57.500 --> 00:04:58.400
Umm...

00:04:59.450 --> 00:05:00.530
What about the kid?

00:05:03.710 --> 00:05:04.790
He's okay.

00:05:05.690 --> 00:05:07.110
At least he's alive.

00:05:10.250 --> 00:05:13.830
I'm glad that the boy and young master are both safe!

00:05:15.100 --> 00:05:16.680
So he was alive.

00:05:17.670 --> 00:05:19.180
Alive...

00:05:22.160 --> 00:05:23.490
Yes.

00:05:24.050 --> 00:05:25.770
He was alive.

00:05:25.770 --> 00:05:27.370
So you were safe...

00:05:42.820 --> 00:05:44.270
The kidnapper was...

00:05:44.270 --> 00:05:46.460
just a young man of 24.

00:05:51.040 --> 00:05:54.180
He couldn't be the man who kidnapped me.

00:06:21.990 --> 00:06:24.440
The more I look,

00:06:24.440 --> 00:06:32.030
the more I realize that this house has
an honorable history as a doctor's residence.

00:06:32.560 --> 00:06:33.660
Anyway,

00:06:34.380 --> 00:06:37.080
the contract is now complete.

00:06:37.080 --> 00:06:40.400
This is one of the best locations in Tokyo.

00:06:40.400 --> 00:06:42.670
It'll make a great apartment.

00:06:43.060 --> 00:06:48.980
If you haven't decided where you're going to live,

00:06:48.980 --> 00:06:51.730
we can introduce you to some brokers.

00:06:54.480 --> 00:06:55.470
Umm?

00:06:56.620 --> 00:06:58.980
I have decided.

00:06:59.830 --> 00:07:01.450
I see.

00:07:01.450 --> 00:07:02.400
Is it in Tokyo?

00:07:03.870 --> 00:07:05.290
Sendai.

00:07:07.760 --> 00:07:09.570
Time went by,

00:07:09.570 --> 00:07:15.350
and the sensational rumors about the kidnappings faded away.

00:07:16.350 --> 00:07:18.540
The shop continues to do well.

00:07:19.410 --> 00:07:20.540
Welcome.

00:07:21.280 --> 00:07:25.710
I'm not that fond of really sweet stuff, so do you have a recommendation?

00:07:25.710 --> 00:07:28.460
Then what about Käse?

00:07:29.370 --> 00:07:34.340
It's a soufflé-type cheesecake, but it's not that sweet.

00:07:34.340 --> 00:07:35.930
I think you'll find it soft and easy to eat.

00:07:36.320 --> 00:07:38.310
Oh, that sounds scrumptious.

00:07:38.310 --> 00:07:39.890
I also like it very much.

00:07:39.890 --> 00:07:41.060
Then I'll try it.

00:07:41.700 --> 00:07:43.270
Certainly.

00:07:46.220 --> 00:07:49.500
Ono-san, Käse is selling well again today.

00:07:49.500 --> 00:07:51.400
There might not be enough for the afternoon.

00:07:51.780 --> 00:07:54.310
Then let's bake some more.

00:07:54.310 --> 00:07:55.590
Kanda-kun?

00:07:55.590 --> 00:07:57.150
Yes, sensei.

00:07:57.150 --> 00:07:59.910
But that Käse really draws a lot of repeat business.

00:07:59.910 --> 00:08:01.440
Yes.

00:08:01.440 --> 00:08:04.380
Even young master had Käse last night.

00:08:05.260 --> 00:08:05.840
What?

00:08:06.640 --> 00:08:08.460
So gramps tried it.

00:08:08.460 --> 00:08:09.570
Yes.

00:08:09.570 --> 00:08:13.940
He said that, in the past, he never wanted to eat cake,

00:08:13.940 --> 00:08:15.340
but that this was good.

00:08:15.340 --> 00:08:16.930
Really?

00:08:19.200 --> 00:08:20.280
Yes.

00:08:23.090 --> 00:08:24.630
The shop is doing very well.

00:08:24.630 --> 00:08:26.400
Sales are as good as they can be.

00:08:26.400 --> 00:08:28.620
Everything is going great.

00:08:28.620 --> 00:08:30.000
Here you are.

00:08:30.000 --> 00:08:31.950
Oh, it looks good!

00:08:32.930 --> 00:08:36.660
I thought that I was all right.

00:08:38.090 --> 00:08:40.530
Käse and cassis for dessert.

00:08:40.530 --> 00:08:41.080
Okay.

00:08:41.420 --> 00:08:44.330
Chi, would you get a container from that shelf?

00:08:44.330 --> 00:08:45.370
Oh, yes.

00:08:45.370 --> 00:08:46.620
W-Will this do?

00:08:47.560 --> 00:08:49.320
What the hell are you doing?

00:08:49.320 --> 00:08:50.770
S-Sorry.

00:08:50.770 --> 00:08:52.730
Chikage-san, are you all right?

00:08:52.730 --> 00:08:54.700
Hey, Chikage. Would you help me?

00:08:54.700 --> 00:08:56.340
Oh, y-yes!

00:09:02.150 --> 00:09:04.050
Hey, Chikage.

00:09:04.050 --> 00:09:06.270
You don't have to sleep that late, even if it's your day off.

00:09:08.910 --> 00:09:10.220
Geez.

00:09:19.000 --> 00:09:19.880
Young master.

00:09:21.900 --> 00:09:22.640
Huh?

00:09:23.180 --> 00:09:24.910
Why are you dressed like that?

00:09:24.910 --> 00:09:26.020
Young master.

00:09:28.770 --> 00:09:30.750
I'll be leaving here today.

00:09:32.310 --> 00:09:33.800
Thank you for your kindness.

00:09:34.980 --> 00:09:36.560
Huh? What?

00:09:36.560 --> 00:09:38.640
Are you going back to my parents' house?

00:09:38.640 --> 00:09:39.610
No.

00:09:40.140 --> 00:09:44.000
I can't trouble the Tachibana family anymore.

00:09:44.000 --> 00:09:47.060
I'm going to live somewhere by myself.

00:09:47.060 --> 00:09:50.440
Oh, I'll still work at your shop of course.

00:09:50.740 --> 00:09:52.740
But why so suddenly?

00:09:53.600 --> 00:09:55.240
Because you're all right.

00:09:55.530 --> 00:09:56.530
What?

00:09:57.410 --> 00:10:01.910
Because you'll be all right without me.

00:10:01.910 --> 00:10:03.270
Well...

00:10:03.270 --> 00:10:05.980
E-Even if that's the case...

00:10:06.480 --> 00:10:08.770
Will you be okay?

00:10:08.770 --> 00:10:09.750
Can you live by yourself?

00:10:10.390 --> 00:10:12.550
You don't have to worry about me.

00:10:12.550 --> 00:10:15.640
I'll call you when I've settled into my new place.

00:10:15.640 --> 00:10:17.590
Please take care of yourself, young master.

00:10:23.270 --> 00:10:25.600
I don't mind...

00:10:26.560 --> 00:10:28.020
but will he really be okay?

00:10:48.320 --> 00:10:49.870
What the...

00:10:49.870 --> 00:10:53.250
I'm not all right in the least.

00:11:04.160 --> 00:11:05.920
Oh yeah, sensei...

00:11:05.920 --> 00:11:08.870
Is it okay if I go to France for a while?

00:11:09.850 --> 00:11:12.370
It's just for two weeks.

00:11:12.830 --> 00:11:18.030
Constance said she's going back to her parents' house tomorrow, and I can go with her.

00:11:18.400 --> 00:11:20.770
Constance?

00:11:20.770 --> 00:11:23.370
Wasn't she your French teacher?

00:11:24.380 --> 00:11:26.100
Oh, yeah,

00:11:26.100 --> 00:11:30.830
and her parents run a bakery near the French border with Spain.

00:11:31.500 --> 00:11:33.460
She told me...

00:11:33.460 --> 00:11:37.640
"Your shop sells very sophisticated sweets,

00:11:37.640 --> 00:11:41.410
but they also taste as tender as my Dad's.

00:11:42.930 --> 00:11:48.110
Your teacher does genuine work and must be a really good pâtissier."

00:11:52.120 --> 00:11:54.960
So, sensei, someday...

00:11:55.630 --> 00:12:00.870
in a few years, I want to go to France and learn about country-style sweets.

00:12:01.480 --> 00:12:05.320
I want to make more heartfelt cakes.

00:12:07.770 --> 00:12:09.440
What? I can't?

00:12:09.890 --> 00:12:11.280
How can...

00:12:11.280 --> 00:12:13.490
Of course you can, Kanda-kun.

00:12:13.490 --> 00:12:17.400
You don't have to worry about the shop at all, so you should go as soon as possible.

00:12:18.490 --> 00:12:19.900
Sensei...

00:12:23.620 --> 00:12:27.310
Geez, Chikage and Eiji...

00:12:27.670 --> 00:12:28.510
What?

00:12:28.510 --> 00:12:31.180
What are you complaining about, gramps?

00:12:31.600 --> 00:12:33.830
Geez, you...

00:12:33.830 --> 00:12:37.780
How can you decide such important things without consulting me, the owner?

00:12:37.780 --> 00:12:39.350
Sorry, Tachibana.

00:12:39.350 --> 00:12:42.680
I was really happy about Kanda-kun's enthusiasm, so...

00:12:42.680 --> 00:12:44.480
It's all right...

00:12:44.480 --> 00:12:46.870
but in return, you'd better study properly.

00:12:46.870 --> 00:12:49.610
Yeah. Thanks, gramps.

00:12:49.610 --> 00:12:51.570
Then, I'm going.

00:12:53.010 --> 00:12:54.110
Have a safe trip.

00:12:54.110 --> 00:12:54.790
Yeah!

00:12:55.880 --> 00:12:56.790
Take care of yourself!

00:12:57.200 --> 00:12:59.210
I'm going!

00:13:01.130 --> 00:13:05.090
I wonder if he's going to leave us when he goes to study abroad eventually.

00:13:05.090 --> 00:13:05.880
Ono-san...

00:13:05.880 --> 00:13:07.140
Don't cry.

00:13:07.140 --> 00:13:08.430
Because...

00:13:08.770 --> 00:13:12.470
Idiot. He'll be coming back soon this time.

00:13:13.040 --> 00:13:14.010
But...

00:13:14.010 --> 00:13:16.700
A grown man crying attracts attention.

00:13:16.700 --> 00:13:18.150
Ono-san, use this.

00:13:18.860 --> 00:13:21.030
Thank you, Chikage-san.

00:13:21.030 --> 00:13:24.520
Please call me and let me know as soon as you've settled in.

00:13:24.520 --> 00:13:26.590
Yes, of course.

00:13:26.590 --> 00:13:28.550
I'll probably move somewhere close to the shop.

00:13:28.980 --> 00:13:30.750
Really? Really, really?

00:13:30.750 --> 00:13:31.550
Yes.

00:13:33.160 --> 00:13:35.510
I've already looked at some properties.

00:13:35.510 --> 00:13:38.810
A place that's close to the shop and to young master.

00:13:40.030 --> 00:13:42.620
Then why are you moving?

00:13:42.620 --> 00:13:44.490
Because young master is all right now.

00:13:44.490 --> 00:13:45.360
Huh?

00:13:46.280 --> 00:13:50.180
No matter what happens, time goes by as usual.

00:13:53.720 --> 00:13:56.560
Oh, isn't it almost lunchtime, Chikage?

00:13:58.690 --> 00:14:01.350
He's off today, too.

00:14:01.350 --> 00:14:04.650
I wonder how long it will take him to move.

00:14:08.230 --> 00:14:10.940
It's kind of deserted here, isn't it?

00:14:12.110 --> 00:14:16.790
Well, Chikage's absence is not that critical a loss, but...

00:14:18.360 --> 00:14:20.290
What? What's up?

00:14:20.750 --> 00:14:22.960
Umm... Nothing.

00:14:23.520 --> 00:14:28.720
I can't quench my thirst without a beautiful garçon here.

00:14:28.720 --> 00:14:30.640
I feel like I'm losing my motivation.

00:14:30.640 --> 00:14:34.270
How can you say that in front of a cool guy like me?!

00:14:37.350 --> 00:14:39.520
We have time to spare. That's unusual.

00:14:40.160 --> 00:14:40.990
Yeah.

00:14:43.040 --> 00:14:44.810
Oh yeah, Tachibana.

00:14:44.810 --> 00:14:50.300
Can I have a day off on Sunday, March 29th?

00:14:50.300 --> 00:14:51.700
Sure, but why?

00:14:52.900 --> 00:14:54.730
It's Nagako's...

00:14:54.730 --> 00:14:58.080
Umm... my sister who came by the other day. It's her wedding.

00:15:00.100 --> 00:15:04.010
I still don't feel good about seeing my mother,

00:15:04.420 --> 00:15:06.920
but I think I should attend.

00:15:07.350 --> 00:15:08.340
I see.

00:15:08.340 --> 00:15:09.540
Yeah.

00:15:09.540 --> 00:15:14.250
And I want to make a wedding cake on that Saturday.

00:15:14.250 --> 00:15:15.290
Is that all right too?

00:15:16.160 --> 00:15:18.050
Of course.

00:15:18.050 --> 00:15:19.450
Thank you.

00:15:19.450 --> 00:15:20.920
Hey, Tachibana...

00:15:20.920 --> 00:15:25.330
Would you have given me a day off if I'd said I want to march in the gay pride parade?

00:15:26.360 --> 00:15:30.000
As long as you didn't go to the parade in your chef's uniform.

00:15:34.090 --> 00:15:35.330
What?

00:15:35.730 --> 00:15:40.830
I just remembered that we were in the same class.

00:15:40.830 --> 00:15:42.480
Oh, I see.

00:15:42.480 --> 00:15:44.180
I've never forgotten that.

00:15:44.180 --> 00:15:46.410
Since our graduation day.

00:15:48.590 --> 00:15:49.760
So...

00:15:55.350 --> 00:15:58.750
I really appreciate what you've done, Tachibana.

00:15:59.320 --> 00:16:04.730
Coming to this shop has made me feel good about being a pâtissier for the first time.

00:16:06.850 --> 00:16:08.410
It's somehow like

00:16:08.410 --> 00:16:13.300
we're back to when we started the shop, with just you and me.

00:16:13.300 --> 00:16:14.210
Yeah.

00:16:15.200 --> 00:16:17.700
I don't know how long this will last,

00:16:18.260 --> 00:16:21.040
but I hope we can continue as long as possible.

00:16:22.040 --> 00:16:26.960
Let's work with great care so we can go on as we have,

00:16:28.340 --> 00:16:30.080
since it won't last forever.

00:16:30.080 --> 00:16:30.380
Yeah.

00:16:34.760 --> 00:16:36.390
It's strange.

00:16:37.220 --> 00:16:42.060
It hasn't been that long since we started the shop,

00:16:42.730 --> 00:16:48.320
but I feel really nostalgic about the time when just the two of us ran it.

00:16:50.190 --> 00:16:52.320
The only thing I'm sure of is

00:16:53.420 --> 00:16:56.360
that we'll never be lovers.

00:16:57.530 --> 00:17:00.790
So we'll never need to break up.

00:17:07.100 --> 00:17:11.000
Let's sell cake enthusiastically today as well!

00:17:11.000 --> 00:17:11.780
Yeah.

00:17:14.190 --> 00:17:15.390
Welcome.

00:17:16.300 --> 00:17:18.100
Have you already decided?

00:17:19.340 --> 00:17:21.640
I want this whole cake.

00:17:22.190 --> 00:17:23.840
Certainly.

00:17:23.840 --> 00:17:26.940
If it's a gift, would you like me to tie a ribbon on it?

00:17:26.940 --> 00:17:29.160
She's not that young,

00:17:29.160 --> 00:17:31.650
so no pink or yellow ribbons.

00:17:31.650 --> 00:17:35.730
Then, how about dark brown?

00:17:35.730 --> 00:17:36.860
That's fine.

00:17:47.530 --> 00:17:48.880
Thank you for waiting.

00:17:53.310 --> 00:17:54.300
Thank you very much.

00:18:21.850 --> 00:18:23.440
W-Wait!

00:18:24.040 --> 00:18:25.900
I won't forgive you!

00:18:25.900 --> 00:18:30.420
I took care of you, but you're such a cruel child!

00:18:30.960 --> 00:18:33.680
Such a terrifying child!

00:18:35.680 --> 00:18:37.760
I-It hurts.

00:18:37.760 --> 00:18:39.860
I-I...

00:18:39.860 --> 00:18:42.780
But... But I have to go home!

00:18:42.780 --> 00:18:44.870
But I...

00:18:44.870 --> 00:18:45.730
I'm sorry!

00:18:46.650 --> 00:18:47.850
I'm sorry...

00:18:47.850 --> 00:18:50.910
I'm sorry... for hurting you!

00:18:54.660 --> 00:18:56.840
A-Are you going to die?

00:18:58.110 --> 00:19:00.160
Are you going to die because of me?

00:19:03.210 --> 00:19:06.270
I killed...

00:19:06.270 --> 00:19:07.270
killed...

00:19:17.010 --> 00:19:18.040
Just go.

00:19:27.250 --> 00:19:28.210
Mister!

00:19:28.210 --> 00:19:29.520
Hurry and go!

00:19:31.310 --> 00:19:33.560
I said I wouldn't forgive you!

00:19:34.240 --> 00:19:35.710
Go away!

00:19:35.710 --> 00:19:37.850
Just go away!

00:19:37.850 --> 00:19:39.930
And forget everything!

00:19:40.820 --> 00:19:42.620
Forget!

00:19:43.140 --> 00:19:47.080
For... get...

00:19:51.430 --> 00:19:52.490
Hurry...

00:19:54.030 --> 00:19:55.800
Go back home.

00:21:13.570 --> 00:21:15.110
The weather's nice.
